Subject: [PATCH] mountmgr: a removable UDisks drive with unknown media is still
 removable

udisks2_add_device() asks UDisks for the drive's MediaCompatibility and maps it
to a device type. For a plain USB mass-storage stick that property is empty, so
the type stays DEVICE_UNKNOWN -- and the drive is then added as a DOS device of
unknown type even though UDisks has just told us, separately, that it is
removable.

The result is that GetDriveTypeW() does not return DRIVE_REMOVABLE for an
ordinary USB stick. Applications that list removable drives therefore never see
it. Measured with rekordbox 7.2.18, whose USB export browser lists only
removable drives: a FAT32 stick was reported as

    E: FIXED  label "REKORDBOX"  fs "NTFS"

and with this patch as

    E: REMOVABLE  label "REKORDBOX"  fs "FAT32"

(The filesystem was misreported as well, but for a different reason: mountmgr
could not open /dev/sda1 to read it -- "get_volume_device_info Failed to open
/dev/sda1, err 5" -- because the device node is root:disk 0660. That is a
packaging matter, not a Wine one.)

device.c already maps DEVICE_HARDDISK to DRIVE_REMOVABLE, so this only makes the
UDisks path agree with the type table that is already there. Windows reports a
USB stick as DRIVE_REMOVABLE.

---
--- a/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c
+++ b/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c
@@ -440,7 +440,28 @@
     }
     if (device)
     {
-        if (removable) queue_device_op( ADD_DOS_DEVICE, udi, device, mount_point, drive_type, guid_ptr, id, label, NULL );
+        if (removable)
+        {
+            /* RBW-REMOVABLE: UDisks has told us the drive is removable. If it
+             * could not also tell us what media it takes -- which is the normal
+             * case for a plain USB mass-storage stick, where
+             * MediaCompatibility is empty -- we were leaving the type as
+             * DEVICE_UNKNOWN, and the application then saw a drive that was not
+             * DRIVE_REMOVABLE. Windows reports a USB stick as DRIVE_REMOVABLE,
+             * and device.c already maps DEVICE_HARDDISK to exactly that, so a
+             * drive UDisks calls removable should be one.
+             *
+             * Measured with rekordbox 7.2.18: its USB export browser lists only
+             * removable drives, so a FAT32 stick that Wine reported as
+             * DRIVE_FIXED never appeared and export was untestable. */
+            if (drive_type == DEVICE_UNKNOWN)
+            {
+                TRACE( "RBW-REMOVABLE %s: removable with unknown media, treating as removable disk\n",
+                       debugstr_a(device) );
+                drive_type = DEVICE_HARDDISK;
+            }
+            queue_device_op( ADD_DOS_DEVICE, udi, device, mount_point, drive_type, guid_ptr, id, label, NULL );
+        }
         else if (guid_ptr) queue_device_op( ADD_VOLUME, udi, device, mount_point, DEVICE_HARDDISK_VOL, guid_ptr, id, label, NULL );
     }
 }
